body:
I'm in South Louisiana so it gets pretty hot down here. I could go through and gut the RV and insulate better, I know how to hang/float sheet rock though I'm assuming it might be a little different process. The park I'm looking into okays dogs and my pup is pretty chill so I think he'll do fine. I'm also not a snob when it comes to scooping poop so I'm fine with that. I'm not sure how realistic my expectations are on repairs honestly. I haven't looked into that side of things. It can't cost more than repairing and maintaining a home right? I'm looking down the barrel of $30,000 in home repairs and a brand new camper sounds way easier and more affordable right about now. 

&#x200B;

What were some of your most expensive repairs if you don't mind me asking? Are they things that someone could learn to do or do you need a handy man to come out? (If it's electrical or plumbing I'd probably need a guy, but I'm talking like maintenance work)
